North Korea is demanding the u.s.  removed Secretary of State Mike Pompeo  from talks over north of the North  Korean nuclear program the country's  foreign minister said overnight they  want to deal with someone who is quote  more careful and mature North Korea also  said it test-fired a new tactical guided  weapon that's the regime's  first such test since President Trump  met with North Korean leader Kim jong-un  earlier this year Ben Tracy is following  these developments from Beijing good  morning North Korea has not provided  many details about what exactly this  weapon is that they've tested but we do  know it is not a ballistic missile it  does not appear to be a weapon that is  capable of striking the United States  now state media in North Korea reports  that North Korean leader Kim jong-un  supervised the test and says the weapon  demonstrated the ability to deliver a  powerful warhead North Korea has not  publicly announced a weapons test since  last November but it appears it is  ramping up its military capabilities  state media released these photos on  wednesday of kim overseeing a flight  drill conducted by the country's air  force now there have also been signs of  activity at North Korean nuclear and  missile production sites this could be a  sign of Kim's frustration with the  diplomacy between him and president  Trump the two failed to reach a  denuclearization agreement at their  summit in Vietnam in February now  president Trump has been defending the  lack of progress at those summits by  saying that North Korea has not been  testing weapons that is now harder to  say Kim jong-un is expected to soon meet  with another world leader Russia's  Vladimir Putin for CBS this morning Ben  Tracy Beijing
 

